Keep exec usable with older pod servers

Allow host upgrades without recreating pods that predate exec and
HTTP/2. Retry the event connection over HTTP/1 when HTTP/2 is
unavailable, and use enter's container transport for those pods before
sending a command. Also fall back when an HTTP/2 pod has no exec
endpoint. Leave stdin unread until execution is accepted, and do not
retry ambiguous execution errors.

Cover the upgrade from the published v0.13.0 release with a real pod,
including its unchanged binary and container ID after the host
upgrade. Check input, arguments, terminal selection, environment,
directory, and exit status through the fallback.
